meta {
  name: App Configs
  seq: 5
}

docs {
  A config is the concrete deployable for an application: container image
  reference + configuration (currently environment variables), targeted at
  exactly one device **or** one group.

  Configs are **immutable and versioned**: updating one creates a new row
  (`version` + 1) and marks the old one `superseded_by` it, so history is
  kept and rollback is possible. A device-specific config beats a group
  config for the same application.
}
